  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture If $G$ is a bridgeless cubic graph, then there exist 6 perfect matchings $M_1,\\ldots,M_6$ of $G$ with the property that every edge of $G$ is contained in exactly two of $M_1,\\ldots,M_6$.",
